!! Authoring and publication sync

The authoring workflow is built around tiddlers tagged `Colleague`. Each colleague tiddler can carry one or more platform identifiers. The plugin then queries enabled providers, caches the responses, and uses DOI matches to connect papers back to people.

!! Supported identifiers

* `orcid`
* `openalex`
* `google-scholar`
* `researcherid`
* `scopus`

!! What happens during sync

* The `/authors/cache` route starts a refresh across all colleague tiddlers.
* Each enabled provider retrieves works for the configured identifiers.
* Cached data is cleaned using TTL and size limits.
* DOI-backed results can be used to tag imported `bibtex-entry` tiddlers with matching authors.

!! Configuration

Open [[$:/plugins/bangyou/tw-pubconnector/settings/authoring]] to control:

* data expiration and cleanup limits
* automatic update schedule
* provider enable or disable flags
* API keys and daily request limits
* Scholar auto-close behavior

!! Notes

* Google Scholar workflows depend on the browser extension because the data is collected through browser navigation.
* ORCID, OpenAlex, Web of Science, and Scopus can be configured directly through plugin settings.
